Z||000000||DecadenceR||07-19-2001||02:20 PM||||I had to replace both driver side cable son my e-brake. HOw do I know when it's properly adjusted? The way i have it now, the brake holds the car in neutral, but not in drive or reverse. I've never needed to adjust one before,so I'm not too clear on this.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||07-19-2001||05:19 PM||||Count the number of clicks until you can't lift the lever any more (don't gorilla-lift it). The 5-7 clicks is about right. Also, with the key in the on position and the brake off, lift the lever and see if the brake light comes on just before the first click.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DecadenceR||07-19-2001||06:54 PM||||heh, I definitely had it too tight, I drove around the block and my brakes were smoking. I took off the wheel and noticed that the lever was about 1/4 inch away from teh caliper. I loosened it up just until it was in the rested position.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
